{"id": "tea:bhaktirasamrtasindhu:1.1.11", "source": "src:bhaktirasamrtasindhu", "location": {"ref": "1.1.11"}, "paraphrase": "The highest devotion (uttamā bhakti) is the cultivation of (activity for) Kṛṣṇa in a favourable spirit, free of desire for anything else and not covered by knowledge (aiming at impersonal oneness), ritual works and the like.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice", "karma-liberation"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "original": {"text": "anyābhilāṣitā-śūnyaṃ jñāna-karmādy-anāvṛtam | ānukūlyena kṛṣṇānuśīlanaṃ bhaktir uttamā ||", "script": "IAST", "edition": "recalled from the standard text (skeleton); verify in Phase D", "licence": "public domain (pre-modern text)"}, "teachers": ["tch:rupa-gosvami"], "concepts": ["cpt:uttama-bhakti"], "terms": ["trm:uttama-bhakti", "trm:anyabhilasita-sunya", "trm:anukulya"], "obstacles": ["obs:anyabhilasa"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:bhaktirasamrtasindhu:1.1.17", "source": "src:bhaktirasamrtasindhu", "location": {"ref": "1.1.17"}, "paraphrase": "Pure devotion destroys suffering, bestows auspiciousness, makes liberation seem trivial, is very rarely attained, is of the nature of intense bliss, and attracts Kṛṣṇa.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "original": {"text": "kleśa-ghnī śubhadā mokṣa-laghutā-kṛt sudurlabhā | sāndrānanda-viśeṣātmā śrī-kṛṣṇākarṣiṇī ca sā ||", "script": "IAST", "edition": "recalled from the standard text (skeleton); verify in Phase D", "licence": "public domain (pre-modern text)"}, "teachers": ["tch:rupa-gosvami"], "concepts": ["cpt:six-characteristics-of-pure-bhakti"], "notes": "Verse number moderately certain.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:bhaktirasamrtasindhu:1.1.23", "source": "src:bhaktirasamrtasindhu", "location": {"ref": "1.1.23"}, "paraphrase": "(Quoting the Padma Purāṇa:) for those devoted to Viṣṇu, sin not yet bearing fruit, sin in its latent stage, its seed, and sin about to bear fruit are destroyed in sequence.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "causal", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:rupa-gosvami"], "concepts": ["cpt:karma-destroyed-by-bhakti"], "notes": "Verse number to verify.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:bhaktirasamrtasindhu:1.2.1-2", "source": "src:bhaktirasamrtasindhu", "location": {"ref": "1.2.1-2"}, "paraphrase": "Devotion is said to be threefold: practice (sādhana), emotion (bhāva) and love (prema). Practice is devotion accomplished by the senses and aiming at bhāva; its attainment is only the manifestation in the heart of an eternally perfect emotion.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all", "stage_native": "sādhana-bhakti"}, "types": ["practice", "karma-liberation"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:rupa-gosvami"], "concepts": ["cpt:three-levels-of-bhakti"], "terms": ["trm:sadhana-bhakti", "trm:bhava-bhakti"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:bhaktirasamrtasindhu:1.2.187", "source": "src:bhaktirasamrtasindhu", "location": {"ref": "1.2.187"}, "paraphrase": "One whose every effort — by action, mind and speech — is for the service of Hari, in all circumstances, is called liberated while living (jīvanmukta).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:rupa-gosvami"], "concepts": ["cpt:jivanmukti"], "disputes": ["dsp:jivanmukti"], "notes": "Verse number to verify.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:bhaktirasamrtasindhu:1.2.22", "source": "src:bhaktirasamrtasindhu", "location": {"ref": "1.2.22"}, "paraphrase": "As long as the witch of desire for enjoyment and liberation remains in the heart, how can the joy of devotion arise there?", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "original": {"text": "bhukti-mukti-spṛhā yāvat piśācī hṛdi vartate | tāvad bhakti-sukhasyātra katham abhyudayo bhavet ||", "script": "IAST", "edition": "recalled from the standard text (skeleton); verify in Phase D", "licence": "public domain (pre-modern text)"}, "teachers": ["tch:rupa-gosvami"], "obstacles": ["obs:bhukti-mukti-sprha"], "notes": "Verse number moderately certain.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:bhaktirasamrtasindhu:1.2.233-234", "source": "src:bhaktirasamrtasindhu", "location": {"ref": "1.2.233-234"}, "paraphrase": "(Quoting the Padma Purāṇa:) the name is a wish-fulfilling gem, Kṛṣṇa himself, the embodiment of consciousness and rasa, complete, pure, eternally free, because the name and the named are non-different. Therefore Kṛṣṇa's name and the rest cannot be grasped by the senses; it manifests of itself on a tongue and senses turned toward service.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["sound-language"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:rupa-gosvami"], "concepts": ["cpt:name-and-named-non-different"], "terms": ["trm:nama"], "notes": "Verse numbers moderately certain.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:bhaktirasamrtasindhu:1.2.255-256", "source": "src:bhaktirasamrtasindhu", "location": {"ref": "1.2.255-256"}, "paraphrase": "Detachment is fitting (yukta-vairāgya) when one uses things as appropriate without attachment, with insistence on their relation to Kṛṣṇa; renunciation of things related to Hari by those seeking liberation, considering them worldly, is called futile detachment (phalgu-vairāgya).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics", "practice"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:rupa-gosvami"], "concepts": ["cpt:yukta-vairagya"], "terms": ["trm:yukta-vairagya"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:bhaktirasamrtasindhu:1.2.270-273", "source": "src:bhaktirasamrtasindhu", "location": {"ref": "1.2.270-273"}, "paraphrase": "Rāgātmikā devotion is that full of rāga — spontaneous, intense absorption in the beloved — as found in the residents of Vraja; devotion that follows it is rāgānugā, of two kinds: following desire (kāmānugā) and following relationship (sambandhānugā).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "intermediate", "stage_native": "rāgānugā sādhana-bhakti"}, "types": ["practice"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:rupa-gosvami"], "concepts": ["cpt:raganuga-bhakti"], "terms": ["trm:ragatmika-bhakti", "trm:raganuga-bhakti"], "notes": "Verse range approximate.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:bhaktirasamrtasindhu:1.2.292", "source": "src:bhaktirasamrtasindhu", "location": {"ref": "1.2.292"}, "paraphrase": "The sign that eager longing (lobha) has arisen is that, on hearing of the sweetness of the Vraja residents' emotions, the mind does not look to scripture or reasoning (for its motive).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:rupa-gosvami"], "concepts": ["cpt:raganuga-bhakti"], "terms": ["trm:lobha"], "notes": "Verse number to verify.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:bhaktirasamrtasindhu:1.2.294-295", "source": "src:bhaktirasamrtasindhu", "location": {"ref": "1.2.294-295"}, "paraphrase": "Remembering Kṛṣṇa and his beloved associate suited to one's own longing, absorbed in their stories, one should always live in Vraja; service is to be done both in the practitioner's form and in the perfected form, by one desiring that emotion, following the people of Vraja.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "original": {"text": "sevā sādhaka-rūpeṇa siddha-rūpeṇa cātra hi | tad-bhāva-lipsunā kāryā vraja-lokānusārataḥ ||", "script": "IAST", "edition": "recalled from the standard text (skeleton); verify in Phase D", "licence": "public domain (pre-modern text)"}, "teachers": ["tch:rupa-gosvami"], "practices": ["prc:raganuga-sadhana", "prc:asta-kaliya-lila-smarana"], "concepts": ["cpt:siddha-deha"], "terms": ["trm:siddha-deha"], "notes": "The quoted original is verse 295.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:bhaktirasamrtasindhu:1.2.6", "source": "src:bhaktirasamrtasindhu", "location": {"ref": "1.2.6"}, "paraphrase": "Where, rāga not having been attained, activity arises only through the command of scripture, that is called devotion by rule (vaidhī bhakti).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "ritual"], "stage": "beginner", "stage_native": "vaidhī sādhana-bhakti"}, "types": ["practice"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:rupa-gosvami"], "concepts": ["cpt:vaidhi-bhakti"], "practices": ["prc:vaidhi-sadhana"], "terms": ["trm:vaidhi-bhakti"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:bhaktirasamrtasindhu:1.2.8", "source": "src:bhaktirasamrtasindhu", "location": {"ref": "1.2.8"}, "paraphrase": "(Quoting the Padma Purāṇa:) Viṣṇu is always to be remembered and never forgotten; all injunctions and prohibitions are servants of these two.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice", "ethics"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:rupa-gosvami"], "notes": "Verse number to verify.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:bhaktirasamrtasindhu:1.2/2", "source": "src:bhaktirasamrtasindhu", "location": {"ref": "1.2"}, "paraphrase": "Rūpa enumerates sixty-four limbs of practice (from taking shelter of a guru's feet, receiving initiation and instruction and serving the guru with trust, through the ten avoidances, to hearing, chanting, remembering and deity service) and names five as most potent: serving the deity with faith, relishing the Bhāgavata with the like-minded, association with advanced devotees, congregational chanting of the name and residence in Mathurā.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "ritual", "sound"], "stage": "beginner", "stage_native": "sādhana-bhakti"}, "types": ["practice"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:rupa-gosvami"], "practices": ["prc:sixty-four-limbs-of-sadhana-bhakti", "prc:five-potent-limbs"], "notes": "Laharī-level reference (the list runs through much of BRS 1.2); verse numbers to supply.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:bhaktirasamrtasindhu:1.3.1", "source": "src:bhaktirasamrtasindhu", "location": {"ref": "1.3.1"}, "paraphrase": "Bhāva is of the nature of special pure sattva, is like a ray of the sun of prema, and softens the heart with tastes (for the Lord).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "advanced", "stage_native": "bhāva-bhakti"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "original": {"text": "śuddha-sattva-viśeṣātmā prema-sūryāṃśu-sāmya-bhāk | rucibhiś citta-māsṛṇya-kṛd asau bhāva ucyate ||", "script": "IAST", "edition": "recalled from the standard text (skeleton); verify in Phase D", "licence": "public domain (pre-modern text)"}, "teachers": ["tch:rupa-gosvami"], "terms": ["trm:bhava"], "concepts": ["cpt:three-levels-of-bhakti"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:bhaktirasamrtasindhu:1.3.25-26", "source": "src:bhaktirasamrtasindhu", "location": {"ref": "1.3.25-26"}, "paraphrase": "In one in whom bhāva has sprouted appear: forbearance, not wasting time, detachment, freedom from pride, hope, eager longing, constant taste for singing the name, attachment to describing his qualities, and affection for his dwelling places.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "advanced", "stage_native": "bhāva-aṅkura"}, "types": ["powers-experiences"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:rupa-gosvami"], "notes": "Verse numbers moderately certain.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:bhaktirasamrtasindhu:1.3/2", "source": "src:bhaktirasamrtasindhu", "location": {"ref": "1.3"}, "paraphrase": "Rūpa distinguishes true bhāva from its semblances (ratyābhāsa), reflected and shadow-like, which appear in those whose hearts are not pure or whose aims are other than devotion; outward signs alone do not prove bhāva.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["powers-experiences"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:rupa-gosvami"], "obstacles": ["obs:ratyabhasa"], "notes": "Laharī-level reference.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:bhaktirasamrtasindhu:1.4.1", "source": "src:bhaktirasamrtasindhu", "location": {"ref": "1.4.1"}, "paraphrase": "When bhāva becomes dense, thoroughly softening the heart and marked by an excess of the sense of possessiveness (mamatā) toward the Lord, the wise call it prema.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "advanced", "stage_native": "prema-bhakti"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "original": {"text": "samyaṅ-masṛṇita-svānto mamatvātiśayāṅkitaḥ | bhāvaḥ sa eva sāndrātmā budhaiḥ premā nigadyate ||", "script": "IAST", "edition": "recalled from the standard text (skeleton); verify in Phase D", "licence": "public domain (pre-modern text)"}, "teachers": ["tch:rupa-gosvami"], "terms": ["trm:prema"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:bhaktirasamrtasindhu:1.4.15-16", "source": "src:bhaktirasamrtasindhu", "location": {"ref": "1.4.15-16"}, "paraphrase": "First faith, then association with saints, then devotional practice, then the removal of unwanted things, then steadiness, then taste, then attachment, then emotion (bhāva), then love (prema) arises: this is the sequence of the appearance of love for practitioners.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice", "karma-liberation"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "original": {"text": "ādau śraddhā tataḥ sādhu-saṅgo 'tha bhajana-kriyā | tato 'nartha-nivṛttiḥ syāt tato niṣṭhā rucis tataḥ || athāsaktis tato bhāvas tataḥ premābhyudañcati | sādhakānām ayaṃ premṇaḥ prādurbhāve bhavet kramaḥ ||", "script": "IAST", "edition": "recalled from the standard text (skeleton); verify in Phase D", "licence": "public domain (pre-modern text)"}, "teachers": ["tch:rupa-gosvami"], "paths": ["pth:rupa-gosvami-bhakti-stages"], "terms": ["trm:sraddha", "trm:sadhu-sanga", "trm:bhajana-kriya", "trm:anartha-nivrtti", "trm:nistha", "trm:ruci", "trm:asakti", "trm:bhava", "trm:prema"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:bhaktirasamrtasindhu:2.1", "source": "src:bhaktirasamrtasindhu", "location": {"ref": "2.1"}, "paraphrase": "Rūpa sets out the components of bhakti-rasa: the permanent emotion (sthāyibhāva, love for Kṛṣṇa) becomes rasa when combined with its excitants (vibhāva: the object, Kṛṣṇa and his devotees, and the stimuli), its outward effects (anubhāva), the involuntary bodily signs (sāttvika) and the transient emotions (vyabhicārin); Kṛṣṇa's sixty-four qualities are described, four unique to him.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:rupa-gosvami"], "concepts": ["cpt:bhakti-rasa-components"], "terms": ["trm:sthayibhava", "trm:vibhava", "trm:anubhava", "trm:sattvika-bhava", "trm:vyabhicari-bhava", "trm:bhakti-rasa"], "notes": "Vibhāga-level reference (southern division, BRS 2.1–2.5).", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:bhaktirasamrtasindhu:2.3", "source": "src:bhaktirasamrtasindhu", "location": {"ref": "2.3"}, "paraphrase": "The eight sāttvika signs — stupor, sweating, horripilation, breaking of the voice, trembling, change of colour, tears and loss of consciousness — appear with degrees of intensity (smouldering, flaming, burning, blazing).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["powers-experiences"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:rupa-gosvami"], "concepts": ["cpt:eight-sattvika-bhavas"], "terms": ["trm:sattvika-bhava"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:bhaktirasamrtasindhu:2.4", "source": "src:bhaktirasamrtasindhu", "location": {"ref": "2.4"}, "paraphrase": "Thirty-three transient emotions (vyabhicārī-bhāva), from despondency (nirveda) to awakening (bodha), rise and fall like waves in the ocean of the permanent emotion.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:rupa-gosvami"], "concepts": ["cpt:thirty-three-vyabhicari-bhavas"], "terms": ["trm:vyabhicari-bhava"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:bhaktirasamrtasindhu:3", "source": "src:bhaktirasamrtasindhu", "location": {"ref": "3"}, "paraphrase": "The five primary devotional rasas are: peaceful (śānta), servitude (prīta/dāsya), friendship (preyas/sakhya), parental affection (vatsala) and amorous love (madhura); each rests on its own permanent emotion toward Kṛṣṇa, and they rise in intensity of relish.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "ultimate"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:rupa-gosvami"], "concepts": ["cpt:five-devotional-rasas"], "terms": ["trm:santa-rasa", "trm:dasya-rasa", "trm:sakhya-rasa", "trm:vatsalya-rasa", "trm:madhura-rasa"], "notes": "Vibhāga-level reference (western division).", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:bhaktirasamrtasindhu:4", "source": "src:bhaktirasamrtasindhu", "location": {"ref": "4"}, "paraphrase": "The seven secondary rasas — humour, wonder, heroism, compassion, anger, fear and disgust — arise within devotion occasionally; mixing incompatible rasas produces only a semblance of rasa (rasābhāsa).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:rupa-gosvami"], "concepts": ["cpt:seven-secondary-rasas"], "terms": ["trm:gauna-rasa", "trm:rasabhasa"], "notes": "Vibhāga-level reference (northern division).", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
